# Apple App Attestation root certificate
#
# Trusting this certificate is what makes an App Attest attestation mean anything: the attestation
# object carries only the credential certificate and the intermediate, so the root is not something
# the evidence can supply. A chain that does not terminate here carries a nonce written by whoever
# produced the chain. Adding or replacing a file in this directory widens what the server accepts
# as hardware backing, so review it as a trust decision rather than as a data update.
#
# Subject      : CN=Apple App Attestation Root CA, O=Apple Inc., ST=California
# Issuer       : CN=Apple App Attestation Root CA, O=Apple Inc., ST=California  (self-signed)
# Serial       : 0BF3BE0EF1CDD2E0FB8C6E721F621798
# Valid        : Mar 18 18:32:53 2020 GMT .. Mar 15 00:00:00 2045 GMT
# SHA-256 (DER), hex       : 1cb9823ba28ba6ad2d33a006941de2ae4f513ef1d4e831b9f7e0fa7b6242c932
# SHA-256 (DER), base64url : HLmCO6KLpq0tM6AGlB3irk9RPvHU6DG59-D6e2JCyTI
#
# Source    : https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/Apple_App_Attestation_Root_CA.pem
#             (listed on https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/private/, retrieved 2026-08-26)
# Reference : https://developer.apple.com/documentation/devicecheck/validating-apps-that-connect-to-your-server
#
# Reproduce and verify:
#   curl -sfL https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/Apple_App_Attestation_Root_CA.pem \
#     | openssl x509 -outform DER | openssl dgst -sha256
#   # expected: 1cb9823ba28ba6ad2d33a006941de2ae4f513ef1d4e831b9f7e0fa7b6242c932
#
# Rotation: Apple has not published a successor. When one appears, add it as a new file rather than
# replacing this one, so devices attested under either root keep verifying, and restate the digest
# in AppleAttestationRootsTest.
#
